"┌ Contents ──────────────┐┌ 17.1 free vs available ────────────────────────────┐"
"│13. Filesystem          ││  ▾ Why is unused RAM wasted RAM?                   │"
"│  13.1 The hierarchy in…││                                                    │"
"│  13.2 /tmp vs /var/tmp ││    RAM is much faster than any disk. When a program│"
"│  13.3 /proc and /sys   ││    reads a file, Linux keeps a copy in the page    │"
"│  13.4 Links, inodes an…││    cache, so the next read comes straight from     │"
"│  13.5 fstab and mount …││    memory. Empty RAM does nothing for you, so the  │"
"│  13.6 /dev and udev    ││    kernel fills it with cache and takes it back    │"
"│14. Disk                ││    when programs ask for memory.                   │"
"│15. Permissions         ││                                                    │"
"│  15.1 rwx, octal and u…││    Taking cache back is cheap when the data is     │"
"│  15.2 setuid, setgid a…││    unchanged: it's still on disk, the kernel can   │"
"│  15.3 sudo and groups  ││    drop it. Changed ("dirty") data must be written │"
"│  15.4 ACLs and capabil…││    to disk first, which is slower.                 │"
"│  15.5 SELinux and AppA…││  ▸ How is "available" calculated?                  │"
"│16. Processes & schedul…││  ▸ What is swappiness and when should I change it? │"
"│  16.1 Process states a…││                                                    │"
"│  16.2 Signals          ││Related                                             │"
"│  16.3 nice and priorit…││  Commands  free, vmstat                            │"
"│  16.4 cgroups          ││  Paths     /proc/meminfo                           │"
